{"title":"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A ride-sharing service calculates fares using the formula:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/4/b345aa651250b000ca1a7d46c8e235fd5e88ae15.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{Total Fare} = \\$1.50\\ \\text{(base fare)} + \\$1.10 \\times (\\text{miles}) + \\$0.25 \\times (\\text{minutes}) + \\$2.00\\ \\text{(booking fee)}\\]\" width=\"637\" height=\"18\" />\nIf a passenger lives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> miles from the airport and estimates the ride will take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> minutes, what is the approximate total fare?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/2/582cb2af54cbb7482e01fb465f261ecc48afdcaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\  \\$20 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\  \\$22 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\  \\$23 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\  \\$25 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\  \\$29 \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"475\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> miles and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> minutes into the formula, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/a/88adc45d466162bf8d040528294aafcbc0fdfc97.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{Total Fare} = \\$1.50 + \\$1.10 \\times 12 + \\$0.25 \\times 20 + \\$2.00 = \\$1.50 + \\$13.20 + \\$5.00 + \\$2.00\\]\" width=\"612\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfc135dac29a9ae149a024e9812288fef05a9b50.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\$14.70 + \\$7.00\\]\" width=\"131\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>This is closest to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/9/bd9b7920b846668e466bc8bdb24e6a03b40fd28f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(B) } \\$22}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"75\" height=\"31\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest\">2025 TMTA Algebra I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Answer_Key\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td 